{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_050 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved 52.0% accuracy / 47.9% F1, but with only one data point I cannot tell whether the image modality, the transformer aggregation, or the weighted fusion is actually contributing beyond what the RNA encoder alone provides. Question: config_010 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is the cleanest single-variable ablation of config_050—it keeps the same RNA encoder (scgpt), same profile setting (multiprofile), and same aggregation (transformer), removing only the image branch. Why this is the best next experiment: establishing the RNA-only baseline is the highest-information experiment at this stage. If RNA alone approaches ~52%, the remaining 8 experiments should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation improvements and the image modality is deprioritized. If RNA alone is substantially lower (e.g., <45%), multimodal fusion is confirmed as a key lever and I should invest remaining budget in fusion strategies and image encoder choices. This single comparison partitions the search space efficiently and prevents wasting experiments on a modality combination that may not be the bottleneck."
}

